  </head>
  <body>
    <SiteHeader />

    <main>
      <section
        class="page-header pillar-hero"
        style="--topic: rgba(241,94,74,0.16); --topic-fg: #d8412c;"
      >
        <div class="container">
          <div class="breadcrumbs">
            <a href="/">Home</a>
            <span>&#8250;</span>
            <a href="/seo">SEO</a>
            <span>&#8250;</span>
            <a href="/seo/backlinks">Link Building</a>
            <span>&#8250;</span>
            <span>Real Estate Posting Sites</span>
          </div>

          <span class="card-icon pillar-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-house-chimney" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
          <p class="eyebrow">Link building</p>
          <h1>{title}</h1>
          <p class="pillar-intro">{intro}</p>
          <PageByline />
          <figure class="posting-feature">
            <img src="/images/posting/real-estate-posting-sites.png" width="1200" height="630" alt={title} loading="eager" />
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="content-body">
        <div class="container article-shell">
          <div class="prose pillar-body">
            <p class="prose-lede">Real estate is not one audience. Agents, investors, landlords, commercial brokers and homebuyers all read different sites and want different things.</p>

            <p>Pitch a property-management blog a homebuyer tip and you will be ignored. Pitch an agent publication an investing deep-dive and same result. The list of 100 is below. First, pick your segment.</p>

            <h2 id="segment">Find your real estate segment first</h2>
            <figure>
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr><th>Your segment</th><th>Best fit on this list</th><th>What they run</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr><td>Agents &amp; brokerages</td><td>Inman, RISMedia, The Close, HousingWire, RealtyTimes</td><td>Industry news, tech reviews, lead-gen and marketing tactics</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Real estate investing</td><td>BiggerPockets, RETipster, InvestFourMore, Coach Carson, Best Ever CRE</td><td>Deal analysis, financing, BRRRR, tax, case studies</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Property management &amp; landlords</td><td>Landlord Station, Rental Housing Journal, Stessa, TurboTenant, Avail</td><td>Screening, leases, maintenance, rent collection, law</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Commercial real estate</td><td>GlobeSt, Bisnow, Commercial Observer, The Real Deal, CoreLogic</td><td>Deals, market data, capital markets, sector trends</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Proptech &amp; tools</td><td>Placester, Carrot, Follow Up Boss, DoorLoop, Buildium</td><td>Product-led how-tos, workflow guides, integrations</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Consumer &amp; home</td><td>HouseLogic, Houzz, Apartment Therapy, HomeLight, ListWithClever</td><td>Buying, selling, moving, home improvement</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>International portals</td><td>Rightmove, Zoopla, realestate.com.au, Domain, 99acres, PropertyGuru</td><td>Local market advice, buying and renting guides</td></tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </figure>

            <h2 id="metrics">What the metrics mean</h2>
            <figure>
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr><th>Metric</th><th>What it is</th><th>How much it matters</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr><td>Domain Rating (DR)</td><td>Ahrefs' 0 to 100 score for a whole site's backlink profile</td><td>A useful filter, not a verdict</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Domain Authority (DA)</td><td>Moz's equivalent 0 to 100 score</td><td>Same idea as DR</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Page Authority (PA)</td><td>Moz's score for one specific page</td><td>Matters once you know which page your post will live on</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>URL Rating (UR)</td><td>Ahrefs' score for one specific URL</td><td>Same purpose as PA</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Monthly Traffic</td><td>Estimated organic visits per month</td><td>The most honest signal that a link will be seen</td></tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </figure>

            <div class="callout"><p><strong>Here is the deal:</strong> the consumer portals at the top of this list have huge traffic but rarely take contributions and rarely pass much relevance to a B2B real estate brand. The agent, investor and property-management sites lower down are where most achievable, useful placements are.</p></div>

            <h2 id="list">The 100 real estate sites</h2>
            <p>Domain Rating, Domain Authority, Page Authority, URL Rating and estimated monthly traffic. Every domain was checked live in September 2026; dead and redirected sites were removed. Metrics are third-party estimates and shift over time.</p>
            <figure>
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr><th>#</th><th>Website</th><th>DR</th><th>DA</th><th>PA</th><th>UR</th><th>Monthly traffic</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  {SITES.map((s) => (
                    <tr>
                      <td>{s.n}</td>
                      <td>{s.site}</td>
                      <td>{s.dr}</td>
                      <td>{s.da}</td>
                      <td>{s.pa}</td>
                      <td>{s.ur}</td>
                      <td>{s.traffic}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </figure>

            <h2 id="pitch">The pitch that works for real estate editors</h2>
            <ol>
              <li><strong>Lead with your standing in the market.</strong> "I'm a broker who closed 40 deals last year" or "we manage 2,000 doors" earns the read.</li>
              <li><strong>Pitch a specific, useful piece.</strong> Not "real estate tips". Something like "the three seller objections that kill a deal in week one, and the scripts that save it".</li>
              <li><strong>Bring numbers.</strong> Local price data, days-on-market trends, portfolio results. Real estate editors love a chart.</li>
              <li><strong>Match the segment's format.</strong> Agent sites want tactical how-tos; investor sites want deal breakdowns; commercial sites want market analysis.</li>
              <li><strong>One clip</strong> in a similar register.</li>
              <li><strong>Disclose any brokerage, CRM or platform you represent.</strong></li>
            </ol>
            <div class="callout"><p><strong>The test:</strong> would an editor commission this from a working agent or investor with nothing to sell? If yes, pitch it. If it is a walkthrough of your product, they will pass.</p></div>

            <h2 id="mistakes">What not to do</h2>
            <ul class="check-list">
              <li>Pitch a generic "tips for first-time buyers" post. Every consumer site has a hundred of those.</li>
              <li>Send the same pitch to an agent blog and a commercial-real-estate outlet. Different readers, different world.</li>
              <li>Stuff the post with links to your listings, your CRM or your lead forms.</li>
              <li>Point exact-match anchors ("best real estate CRM") at your own product page.</li>
              <li>Submit AI-spun filler with no local knowledge or real numbers. It stands out immediately in this niche.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="callout"><p><strong>Bottom line:</strong> a few placements on the sites your segment actually reads will do more for your rankings and your reputation than a long list of high-DR portal links. Use this list to find your few.</p></div>
          </div>

          <aside class="article-toc">
            <h4>On this page</h4>
            <ul>
              {toc.map((item) => (
                <li><a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.text}</a></li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div id="faq">
        <Faq items={faqs} />
      </div>

      <section class="section section-alt">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="cta-panel" style="text-align: center; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto;">
            <h2>Want us to run the outreach?</h2>
            <p>
              We build the shortlist by segment, write the pitches and the pieces, and place them
              on relevant real estate sites with real editorial standards. No link farms, no risk.
            </p>
            <div class="hero-actions" style="justify-content: center; margin-top: 0;">
              <a href="/services" class="button">View services</a>
              <a
                href={whatsappUrl("Hi SERP Mentor, I would like help with real estate guest posting and digital PR.")}
                class="button-secondary"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                <i class="fa-brands fa-whatsapp" aria-hidden="true"></i> WhatsApp
              </a>
            </div>
